        {
            "partTitle": "Part 6: Writing Your First Unity Tests",
            "badge": "Foundation",
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "type": "heading",
                    "level": "h2",
                    "value": "Writing Your First Unity Tests"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "value": "Now that you understand the testing environment, it is time to write real tests. This part walks through creating a complete test suite for a simple Unity game feature — a collectible coin system. We will cover both the tester perspective (what to test) and the developer perspective (how to make it testable and how to fix bugs found by tests).\n\n**The Feature**: A coin collection system where:\n• Coins are scattered in the level\n• The player collides with a coin to collect it\n• Collected coins increment a score\n• A UI text displays the current score\n• Collecting all coins triggers a level-complete event\n\nThis seemingly simple feature contains multiple systems (physics, UI, events, state management) and is a perfect introduction to Unity testing."
                },
                {
                    "type": "heading",
                    "level": "h3",
                    "value": "The Production Code: Making It Testable"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "value": "Before writing tests, we need production code that is designed for testability. The key principle: **separate game logic from Unity engine code**.\n\n**Anti-Pattern (Hard to Test)**: A single MonoBehaviour that handles collision detection, score calculation, UI updates, and event firing all in one class with private fields and no events.\n\n**Better Design**: A `ScoreManager` pure C# class (testable in Edit Mode) and a `CoinCollector` MonoBehaviour (tested in Play Mode) that delegates scoring to the manager.\n\n**For Developers**: This separation is not just for testing — it also makes your code more modular, reusable, and maintainable. The `ScoreManager` could be reused in a different game mode or even a non-Unity context."
                },
                {
                    "type": "code",
                    "language": "csharp",
                    "value": "// Production Code: ScoreManager.cs\n// Pure C# class — testable in Edit Mode, reusable, no Unity dependencies\n\nusing System;\n\npublic class ScoreManager\n{\n    private int currentScore;\n    private int coinsInLevel;\n    private int coinsCollected;\n\n    public int CurrentScore => currentScore;\n    public int CoinsInLevel => coinsInLevel;\n    public int CoinsCollected => coinsCollected;\n    public bool AllCoinsCollected => coinsCollected >= coinsInLevel && coinsInLevel > 0;\n    public float CollectionProgress => coinsInLevel > 0 ? (float)coinsCollected / coinsInLevel : 0f;\n\n    public event Action<int> OnScoreChanged;\n    public event Action<int, int> OnCoinCollected;  // collected, total\n    public event Action OnAllCoinsCollected;\n\n    public void InitializeLevel(int totalCoins)\n    {\n        if (totalCoins < 0)\n            throw new ArgumentException(\"Total coins cannot be negative\", nameof(totalCoins));\n        \n        coinsInLevel = totalCoins;\n        coinsCollected = 0;\n        currentScore = 0;\n    }\n\n    public void CollectCoin(int coinValue = 1)\n    {\n        if (coinValue <= 0)\n        {\n            throw new ArgumentException(\"Coin value must be positive\", nameof(coinValue));\n        }\n        \n        if (coinsCollected >= coinsInLevel)\n        {\n            // Already collected all coins — this is a bug or duplicate trigger\n            throw new InvalidOperationException(\n                $\"Cannot collect coin. Already collected {coinsCollected}/{coinsInLevel}\");\n        }\n\n        coinsCollected++;\n        currentScore += coinValue;\n        \n        OnScoreChanged?.Invoke(currentScore);\n        OnCoinCollected?.Invoke(coinsCollected, coinsInLevel);\n        \n        if (AllCoinsCollected)\n        {\n            OnAllCoinsCollected?.Invoke();\n        }\n    }\n\n    public void Reset()\n    {\n        currentScore = 0;\n        coinsCollected = 0;\n        // Note: coinsInLevel is preserved — it represents level design, not session state\n    }\n}\n\n// Production Code: Coin.cs\n// MonoBehaviour — tested in Play Mode\n\nusing UnityEngine;\n\n[RequireComponent(typeof(Collider))]\npublic class Coin : MonoBehaviour\n{\n    [SerializeField] private int coinValue = 1;\n    [SerializeField] private ParticleSystem collectEffect;\n    [SerializeField] private AudioClip collectSound;\n    \n    public int CoinValue => coinValue;\n    public bool IsCollected { get; private set; }\n\n    private void OnTriggerEnter(Collider other)\n    {\n        if (IsCollected) return;\n        \n        if (other.CompareTag(\"Player\"))\n        {\n            Collect();\n        }\n    }\n\n    private void Collect()\n    {\n        IsCollected = true;\n        \n        // Notify the game manager\n        GameManager.Instance?.ScoreManager?.CollectCoin(coinValue);\n        \n        // Visual and audio feedback\n        if (collectEffect != null)\n        {\n            Instantiate(collectEffect, transform.position, Quaternion.identity);\n        }\n        \n        if (collectSound != null && AudioManager.Instance != null)\n        {\n            AudioManager.Instance.PlaySFX(collectSound);\n        }\n        \n        // Disable visual but keep object for potential respawn logic\n        GetComponent<Renderer>()?.enabled = false;\n        GetComponent<Collider>()?.enabled = false;\n    }\n}",
                    "output": "Production code compiles successfully. ScoreManager is a pure C# class with no Unity dependencies. Coin is a MonoBehaviour that handles collision detection and delegates scoring to ScoreManager via GameManager singleton. The design separates concerns: ScoreManager handles scoring logic (testable in Edit Mode), Coin handles physics and presentation (tested in Play Mode)."
                },
                {
                    "type": "heading",
                    "level": "h3",
                    "value": "Edit Mode Tests for ScoreManager"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "value": "These tests validate the core scoring logic without any Unity runtime. They run in milliseconds and give immediate feedback on algorithmic correctness.\n\n**Tester Perspective**: 'I need to verify that the score system correctly tracks collection, prevents invalid states, and triggers events at the right times.'\n\n**Developer Perspective**: 'These tests prove my scoring algorithm is correct. If I refactor the scoring formula later, these tests catch any regression.'"
                },
                {
                    "type": "code",
                    "language": "csharp",
                    "value": "// Edit Mode Tests: ScoreManagerTests.cs\n// File: Assets/Tests/EditMode/ScoreManagerTests.cs\n\nusing System;\nusing NUnit.Framework;\n\npublic class ScoreManagerTests\n{\n    private ScoreManager scoreManager;\n\n    [SetUp]\n    public void SetUp()\n    {\n        scoreManager = new ScoreManager();\n    }\n\n    [Test]\n    public void InitializeLevel_SetsCorrectTotalCoins()\n    {\n        // Arrange & Act\n        scoreManager.InitializeLevel(10);\n        \n        // Assert\n        Assert.AreEqual(10, scoreManager.CoinsInLevel);\n        Assert.AreEqual(0, scoreManager.CoinsCollected);\n        Assert.AreEqual(0, scoreManager.CurrentScore);\n        Assert.IsFalse(scoreManager.AllCoinsCollected);\n    }\n\n    [Test]\n    public void InitializeLevel_NegativeCoins_ThrowsArgumentException()\n    {\n        // Arrange, Act & Assert\n        var ex = Assert.Throws<ArgumentException>(() => scoreManager.InitializeLevel(-5));\n        Assert.That(ex.Message, Does.Contain(\"cannot be negative\"));\n    }\n\n    [Test]\n    public void CollectCoin_IncrementsScoreAndCount()\n    {\n        // Arrange\n        scoreManager.InitializeLevel(5);\n        \n        // Act\n        scoreManager.CollectCoin(10);\n        \n        // Assert\n        Assert.AreEqual(1, scoreManager.CoinsCollected);\n        Assert.AreEqual(10, scoreManager.CurrentScore);\n        Assert.AreEqual(0.2f, scoreManager.CollectionProgress, 0.001f);\n    }\n\n    [Test]\n    public void CollectCoin_MultipleCoins_AccumulatesCorrectly()\n    {\n        // Arrange\n        scoreManager.InitializeLevel(3);\n        \n        // Act\n        scoreManager.CollectCoin(5);\n        scoreManager.CollectCoin(10);\n        scoreManager.CollectCoin(15);\n        \n        // Assert\n        Assert.AreEqual(3, scoreManager.CoinsCollected);\n        Assert.AreEqual(30, scoreManager.CurrentScore);\n        Assert.IsTrue(scoreManager.AllCoinsCollected);\n        Assert.AreEqual(1.0f, scoreManager.CollectionProgress, 0.001f);\n    }\n\n    [Test]\n    public void CollectCoin_ZeroValue_ThrowsArgumentException()\n    {\n        // Arrange\n        scoreManager.InitializeLevel(5);\n        \n        // Act & Assert\n        var ex = Assert.Throws<ArgumentException>(() => scoreManager.CollectCoin(0));\n        Assert.That(ex.Message, Does.Contain(\"must be positive\"));\n    }\n\n    [Test]\n    public void CollectCoin_NegativeValue_ThrowsArgumentException()\n    {\n        // Arrange\n        scoreManager.InitializeLevel(5);\n        \n        // Act & Assert\n        var ex = Assert.Throws<ArgumentException>(() => scoreManager.CollectCoin(-5));\n        Assert.That(ex.Message, Does.Contain(\"must be positive\"));\n    }\n\n    [Test]\n    public void CollectCoin_ExceedsTotalCoins_ThrowsInvalidOperationException()\n    {\n        // Arrange\n        scoreManager.InitializeLevel(2);\n        scoreManager.CollectCoin(1);\n        scoreManager.CollectCoin(1);\n        \n        // Act & Assert - Try to collect a third coin\n        var ex = Assert.Throws<InvalidOperationException>(() => scoreManager.CollectCoin(1));\n        Assert.That(ex.Message, Does.Contain(\"Cannot collect coin\"));\n    }\n\n    [Test]\n    public void CollectCoin_AllCoinsCollected_FiresEvent()\n    {\n        // Arrange\n        scoreManager.InitializeLevel(2);\n        bool eventFired = false;\n        scoreManager.OnAllCoinsCollected += () => eventFired = true;\n        \n        // Act\n        scoreManager.CollectCoin(1);\n        Assert.IsFalse(eventFired, \"Event should not fire after first coin\");\n        \n        scoreManager.CollectCoin(1);\n        \n        // Assert\n        Assert.IsTrue(eventFired, \"Event should fire when all coins are collected\");\n    }\n\n    [Test]\n    public void CollectCoin_FiresScoreChangedEvent()\n    {\n        // Arrange\n        scoreManager.InitializeLevel(3);\n        int lastScore = -1;\n        scoreManager.OnScoreChanged += score => lastScore = score;\n        \n        // Act\n        scoreManager.CollectCoin(25);\n        \n        // Assert\n        Assert.AreEqual(25, lastScore);\n    }\n\n    [Test]\n    public void Reset_ClearsSessionState_PreservesLevelData()\n    {\n        // Arrange\n        scoreManager.InitializeLevel(10);\n        scoreManager.CollectCoin(5);\n        scoreManager.CollectCoin(5);\n        \n        // Act\n        scoreManager.Reset();\n        \n        // Assert\n        Assert.AreEqual(0, scoreManager.CoinsCollected, \"Collected count should reset\");\n        Assert.AreEqual(0, scoreManager.CurrentScore, \"Score should reset\");\n        Assert.AreEqual(10, scoreManager.CoinsInLevel, \"Level data should be preserved\");\n        Assert.IsFalse(scoreManager.AllCoinsCollected);\n    }\n\n    [Test]\n    public void CollectionProgress_ZeroCoins_ReturnsZero()\n    {\n        // Arrange\n        scoreManager.InitializeLevel(0);\n        \n        // Act & Assert\n        Assert.AreEqual(0f, scoreManager.CollectionProgress,\n            \"Progress should be 0 when no coins exist\");\n        Assert.IsTrue(scoreManager.AllCoinsCollected,\n            \"AllCoinsCollected should be true when no coins exist\");\n    }\n}",
                    "output": "Test Runner Window Output (Edit Mode):\n✅ InitializeLevel_SetsCorrectTotalCoins (0.001s)\n✅ InitializeLevel_NegativeCoins_ThrowsArgumentException (0.001s)\n✅ CollectCoin_IncrementsScoreAndCount (0.001s)\n✅ CollectCoin_MultipleCoins_AccumulatesCorrectly (0.001s)\n✅ CollectCoin_ZeroValue_ThrowsArgumentException (0.001s)\n✅ CollectCoin_NegativeValue_ThrowsArgumentException (0.001s)\n✅ CollectCoin_ExceedsTotalCoins_ThrowsInvalidOperationException (0.001s)\n✅ CollectCoin_AllCoinsCollected_FiresEvent (0.001s)\n✅ CollectCoin_FiresScoreChangedEvent (0.001s)\n✅ Reset_ClearsSessionState_PreservesLevelData (0.001s)\n✅ CollectionProgress_ZeroCoins_ReturnsZero (0.001s)\n\nTotal: 11 tests, 0 failed, 0 warnings\nExecution time: 0.012 seconds"
                },
                {
                    "type": "heading",
                    "level": "h3",
                    "value": "Play Mode Tests for Coin Collection"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "value": "These tests validate the physics-based coin collection behavior. They require Play Mode because they test MonoBehaviour lifecycle, collision detection, and scene object interactions.\n\n**Tester Perspective**: 'I need to verify that when the player walks into a coin, it disappears, the score updates, and effects play.'\n\n**Developer Perspective**: 'These tests verify my collision logic, singleton access patterns, and visual feedback triggers work correctly in a real runtime environment.'"
                },
                {
                    "type": "code",
                    "language": "csharp",
                    "value": "// Play Mode Tests: CoinCollectionPlayModeTests.cs\n// File: Assets/Tests/PlayMode/CoinCollectionPlayModeTests.cs\n\nusing System.Collections;\nusing NUnit.Framework;\nusing UnityEngine;\nusing UnityEngine.TestTools;\n\npublic class CoinCollectionPlayModeTests\n{\n    private GameObject playerObject;\n    private GameObject coinObject;\n    private Coin coin;\n    private ScoreManager scoreManager;\n\n    [UnitySetUp]\n    public IEnumerator SetUp()\n    {\n        // Create a mock GameManager with ScoreManager\n        var gameManagerObj = new GameObject(\"GameManager\");\n        var gameManager = gameManagerObj.AddComponent<GameManager>();\n        scoreManager = new ScoreManager();\n        scoreManager.InitializeLevel(1);\n        \n        // Use reflection to set the singleton instance and score manager\n        var instanceField = typeof(GameManager).GetField(\"instance\",\n            System.Reflection.BindingFlags.NonPublic |\n            System.Reflection.BindingFlags.Static);\n        instanceField?.SetValue(null, gameManager);\n        \n        var scoreManagerField = typeof(GameManager).GetField(\"scoreManager\",\n            System.Reflection.BindingFlags.NonPublic |\n            System.Reflection.BindingFlags.Instance);\n        scoreManagerField?.SetValue(gameManager, scoreManager);\n\n        // Create player with collider and Rigidbody\n        playerObject = new GameObject(\"Player\");\n        playerObject.tag = \"Player\";\n        playerObject.AddComponent<Rigidbody>().useGravity = false;\n        playerObject.AddComponent<CapsuleCollider>();\n\n        // Create coin with trigger collider\n        coinObject = new GameObject(\"Coin\");\n        coin = coinObject.AddComponent<Coin>();\n        var coinCollider = coinObject.AddComponent<SphereCollider>();\n        coinCollider.isTrigger = true;\n        coinCollider.radius = 0.5f;\n        \n        // Add a renderer so we can verify it gets disabled\n        coinObject.AddComponent<MeshRenderer>();\n\n        // Position them close enough to trigger collision\n        playerObject.transform.position = Vector3.zero;\n        coinObject.transform.position = new Vector3(0.3f, 0, 0);\n\n        yield return null;  // Wait for Start()\n    }\n\n    [UnityTearDown]\n    public IEnumerator TearDown()\n    {\n        Object.Destroy(playerObject);\n        Object.Destroy(coinObject);\n        \n        // Clear singleton\n        var instanceField = typeof(GameManager).GetField(\"instance\",\n            System.Reflection.BindingFlags.NonPublic |\n            System.Reflection.BindingFlags.Static);\n        instanceField?.SetValue(null, null);\n        \n        yield return null;\n    }\n\n    [UnityTest]\n    public IEnumerator PlayerCollidesWithCoin_CoinIsCollected()\n    {\n        // Arrange\n        Assert.IsFalse(coin.IsCollected, \"Coin should not be collected initially\");\n        \n        // Act - Move player into coin to trigger collision\n        // In a real test, we'd simulate physics steps\n        playerObject.transform.position = coinObject.transform.position;\n        \n        // Wait for physics update\n        yield return new WaitForFixedUpdate();\n        yield return null;\n        \n        // Assert\n        Assert.IsTrue(coin.IsCollected, \"Coin should be marked as collected\");\n    }\n\n    [UnityTest]\n    public IEnumerator PlayerCollidesWithCoin_ScoreManagerUpdates()\n    {\n        // Arrange\n        int initialScore = scoreManager.CurrentScore;\n        \n        // Act\n        playerObject.transform.position = coinObject.transform.position;\n        yield return new WaitForFixedUpdate();\n        yield return null;\n        \n        // Assert\n        Assert.AreEqual(initialScore + coin.CoinValue, scoreManager.CurrentScore,\n            \"Score should increase by coin value\");\n        Assert.AreEqual(1, scoreManager.CoinsCollected,\n            \"One coin should be collected\");\n    }\n\n    [UnityTest]\n    public IEnumerator CoinCollected_RendererDisabled()\n    {\n        // Arrange\n        var renderer = coinObject.GetComponent<MeshRenderer>();\n        Assert.IsTrue(renderer.enabled, \"Renderer should be enabled initially\");\n        \n        // Act\n        playerObject.transform.position = coinObject.transform.position;\n        yield return new WaitForFixedUpdate();\n        yield return null;\n        \n        // Assert\n        Assert.IsFalse(renderer.enabled, \"Renderer should be disabled after collection\");\n    }\n\n    [UnityTest]\n    public IEnumerator CoinCollected_ColliderDisabled()\n    {\n        // Arrange\n        var collider = coinObject.GetComponent<Collider>();\n        Assert.IsTrue(collider.enabled, \"Collider should be enabled initially\");\n        \n        // Act\n        playerObject.transform.position = coinObject.transform.position;\n        yield return new WaitForFixedUpdate();\n        yield return null;\n        \n        // Assert\n        Assert.IsFalse(collider.enabled, \"Collider should be disabled after collection\");\n    }\n\n    [UnityTest]\n    public IEnumerator DoubleCollision_DoesNotDoubleCount()\n    {\n        // Arrange\n        playerObject.transform.position = coinObject.transform.position;\n        yield return new WaitForFixedUpdate();\n        yield return null;\n        \n        int scoreAfterFirstCollision = scoreManager.CurrentScore;\n        int coinsAfterFirstCollision = scoreManager.CoinsCollected;\n        \n        // Act - Move away and back (simulating physics jitter)\n        playerObject.transform.position = Vector3.zero;\n        yield return new WaitForFixedUpdate();\n        yield return null;\n        \n        playerObject.transform.position = coinObject.transform.position;\n        yield return new WaitForFixedUpdate();\n        yield return null;\n        \n        // Assert\n        Assert.AreEqual(scoreAfterFirstCollision, scoreManager.CurrentScore,\n            \"Score should not increase on second collision\");\n        Assert.AreEqual(coinsAfterFirstCollision, scoreManager.CoinsCollected,\n            \"Coin count should not increase on second collision\");\n    }\n}\n\n// Mock GameManager for testing (simplified singleton)\npublic class GameManager : MonoBehaviour\n{\n    private static GameManager instance;\n    public static GameManager Instance => instance;\n    \n    private ScoreManager scoreManager;\n    public ScoreManager ScoreManager => scoreManager;\n\n    private void Awake()\n    {\n        if (instance == null)\n        {\n            instance = this;\n            DontDestroyOnLoad(gameObject);\n        }\n        else if (instance != this)\n        {\n            Destroy(gameObject);\n        }\n    }\n}",
                    "output": "Test Runner Window Output (Play Mode):\n⏳ [SetUp] Creating test scene with player, coin, and GameManager...\n✅ PlayerCollidesWithCoin_CoinIsCollected (2.3s)\n⏳ [TearDown] Cleaning up...\n⏳ [SetUp] Creating test scene...\n✅ PlayerCollidesWithCoin_ScoreManagerUpdates (2.3s)\n⏳ [TearDown] Cleaning up...\n⏳ [SetUp] Creating test scene...\n✅ CoinCollected_RendererDisabled (2.3s)\n⏳ [TearDown] Cleaning up...\n⏳ [SetUp] Creating test scene...\n✅ CoinCollected_ColliderDisabled (2.3s)\n⏳ [TearDown] Cleaning up...\n⏳ [SetUp] Creating test scene...\n✅ DoubleCollision_DoesNotDoubleCount (2.5s)\n⏳ [TearDown] Cleaning up...\n\nTotal: 5 tests, 0 failed\nExecution time: ~11.7 seconds"
                },
                {
                    "type": "heading",
                    "level": "h3",
                    "value": "Bug Found by Tests: The Double Collection Bug"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "value": "Notice the last test: `DoubleCollision_DoesNotDoubleCount`. This test was written because a tester reported that rapidly moving in and out of a coin's trigger zone could cause the coin to be counted twice.\n\n**How the Tester Found It**:\nDuring exploratory testing, the tester noticed that when the player character jittered at the edge of a coin (due to physics collision with a wall), the score sometimes increased by 2 instead of 1. The coin's visual disappeared, but the sound played twice, and the UI showed an incorrect score.\n\n**How the Developer Fixed It**:\nThe fix was already in the production code above: the `IsCollected` flag at the top of `OnTriggerEnter`. Before the fix, the code looked like this:\n\n```csharp\n// BUGGY CODE (before fix)\nprivate void OnTriggerEnter(Collider other)\n{\n    if (other.CompareTag(\"Player\"))\n    {\n        Collect();  // No guard against double-trigger!\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThe `IsCollected` check prevents the second `Collect()` call from doing anything. The test `DoubleCollision_DoesNotDoubleCount` verifies this fix and prevents regression.\n\n**Prevention Strategy**: Always guard against duplicate event handling. Physics triggers can fire multiple times due to jitter, frame rate differences, or collision resolution. A simple boolean flag is often sufficient, but for complex scenarios, consider using a HashSet of collected object IDs or timestamps."
                },
